{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 37","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The base of an isosceles triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> inches and one of the equal sides is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> inches. \nThe radius of the circle through the vertices of the triangle is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e0d5922a81374f064dc864e33ca09885c9530c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{7\\sqrt{15}}{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 4\\sqrt{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3\\sqrt{5} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\sqrt{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"545\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/4/d348f55d6eb6e863395a6ba14e560a060ec7e291.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(3,3sqrt(15))--(6,0)--cycle); draw((3,3sqrt(15))--(3,0)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(3,3sqrt(15)),N); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(0,0),SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(6,0),SE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(3,0),S); label(&quot;12&quot;,(1.5,5.8),WNW); label(&quot;12&quot;,(4.5,5.8),ENE); label(&quot;3&quot;,(1.5,0),N); [/asy]\" width=\"152\" height=\"252\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> be an isosceles triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/6/516802cbd04930f9695d81be2805a72476c626f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=AC=12,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/f/4ff67bed50815f029660d4da83fcd8b16c9f9176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />. Draw altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is the apex of the triangle, the altitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/b/cfbb4c52e011ceed6e813118a7d59e931af444a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AD}$\" width=\"29\" height=\"15\" /> is also a median of the triangle. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af1004dda308528b877da5e7a63eb52db4a388c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD=CD=3$\" width=\"117\" height=\"12\" />. Using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pythagorean_Theorem\" title=\"Pythagorean Theorem\">Pythagorean Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/7/0b7291c43c0d24a545684b29b2dbb03b380d0514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=\\sqrt{12^2-3^2}=3\\sqrt{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"200\" height=\"19\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/6/7c6b00799bb20a430f3b02d1ef0b0fb6ec307712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac12\\cdot 6\\cdot 3\\sqrt{15}=9\\sqrt{15}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"158\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/b/a5b29b358e825defa3e11b7d903d43ec31e5909a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> are the sides of a triangle, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is its area, the circumradius of that triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56ca5132df9de4ecbf61bafb572e0b57ff8a183.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{abc}{4A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"31\" height=\"39\" />. Using this formula, we find the circumradius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/031100234ae516e8ff0c42099766b9b2bde53fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{6\\cdot 12\\cdot 12}{4\\cdot 9\\sqrt{15}}=\\frac{2\\cdot 12}{\\sqrt{15}}=\\frac{24\\sqrt{15}}{15}=\\frac{8\\sqrt{15}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"293\" height=\"45\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f02753f9a328103e8713e63ba165e4d8e2d432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"140\" height=\"28\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_37&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME\" title=\"1953 AHSME\">1953 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1953 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1953\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_36\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 36\">Problem 36</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_38\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 38\">Problem 38</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1953 AHSME Pro